  "maximized_paper_summary": "After these revisions, the strongest faithful paper would derive cost-optimal source allocation for each regular bridge design, establish pilot selection and independent-main-sample inference, and prove that a genuinely unequal-cost predictive selector can be arbitrarily inefficient because inverse selection-bridge geometry deteriorates while every candidate remains pointwise identified and regular. It would also state sharply that finiteness supplies only a law-specific enumerated ratio unless additional primitive operator comparability is imposed.",
